   "name": "Vault Door Freight Recovery Case Study — Manassas, VA (September 2026)",
   "description": "The structured case record of one real vault door job, published as data: in September 2026 a reconditioned vault door — 1,475 lbs on one pallet at 41 × 41 × 42 inches, cube 40.86 cubic feet, density 36.1 PCF, freight class 60, NMFC 172360-11, prepaid — was shipped by LTL freight to a carrier terminal in Manassas, VA and held will-call. The Flat Rate Movers' Winchester branch crew recovered it at the loading dock inside the 7:30 AM – 2:00 PM pickup window, ran the final-mile leg to the client, and placed the door under the white-glove standard. The dataset carries the complete end-to-end process as seven structured steps, each mapped to the registered service that performed it, the full transcribed freight record, and the evidence block: the document types and dates behind every figure, with the density cross-check (1,475 lbs ÷ 40.86 cu ft = 36.1 PCF) verified against the bill of lading. Names of individuals, the seller and the client are withheld under the company's privacy rule; geography is published at city level.",
